.SH FILES
Files live in %APPDATA%\etarion on Windows, ~/.config/tarion on Linux and ~/Library/Application Support/tarion on macOS, or in \fB$TARION_HOME\fR.
.TP
\fIconfig.json\fR
settings and contacts
.TP
\fIidentity.key\fR
this device's private key (encrypted)
.TP
\fIvault.json\fR
the data key, protected by the Windows login or a passphrase
.TP
\fIpeers.json\fR
pinned contacts and their verified devices
.TP
\fIhistory/\fR
one chat per file
.TP
\fIoutbox.json\fR
messages waiting to be delivered
.TP
\fIdropped.log\fR
messages given up on or refused
.TP
\fIrevoked.json\fR
keys the server banned
.TP
\fIbackground.log\fR
the background process's log
.TP
\fIcontrol.token\fR
the local API secret, while the background process runs
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTARION_HOME\fR
use another folder, e.g. a second identity on one machine
.TP
\fBTARION_NO_AUTO_PROTECT\fR
set to 1 to not encrypt a new Windows install automatically
.TP
\fBTARION_SIMULATE_STRICT_NAT\fR
set to 1 to drop direct packets from peers (testing)
.SH PORTS
One UDP port for chat and the server (default 63426, \fB\-p\fR); the background control socket listens on 127.0.0.1, by default that port plus 10000 (\fB\-cp\fR). tariond listens on UDP 63425.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on an error, which is printed to standard error with what to do about it.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtariond\fR(8), \fBtarion help\fR, https://github.com/necromancer124/tarion
